    "source": {
      "provider": "GenshinOptimizer+ProjectAmber",
      "goSheet": "libs/gi/sheets/src/Characters/Chasca",
      "notes": "Shell/ShiningShell/Radiant hits modelled as base Anemo, with per-element variants (_pyro/_hydro/_electro/_cryo) added 2026-07-24 to match GO's objKeyMap(absorbableEle,...) sheet structure and the rotation paths several existing local leaderboards already reference (skill.shiningShellDmg_<elem>, burst.radiantDmg_<elem>) -- these were previously unresolvable (0 dmg). Also added per GO's sheet: constellation2/constellation4 sections (C2 'Muzzle, the Searing Smoke' / C4 'Sparks, the Sudden Shot', each atk x4.0, anemo + 4 elemental variants, 'charged' dmg type per GO -- supersedes the old anemo-only skill.c2MuzzleDmg/burst.c4SparksDmg keys, which no leaderboard referenced) and a passive2 section (A4 'Intent to Cover': fires a Burning Shadowhunt Shot dealing 150% of the triggering Shell/Shining Shell's DMG -- shellDmg_mult x1.5 for anemo, shiningShellDmg_mult x1.5 for the elemental variants). C2/C4/A4 require the matching unlock -- there's no in-file constellation/ascension gate on hit_definitions, so only include these rotation targets in leaderboards that assume the matching unlock. 2026-08-04: the skill.shiningShellDmg* hits also carry a bespoke `shiningshell_dmg_` bonus key so A1 (Bullet Trick) can buff the Shining Shadowhunt Shell alone -- every other hit here tagged 'charged' (aimed/fullyAimed, constellation2, constellation4, passive2) is a Charged Attack but NOT a Shining Shell, and must not carry that key.",
      "assumptions": {
        "constellation": 0,
        "characterLevel": 90,
        "autoTalentLevel": 10,
        "skillTalentLevel": 10,
        "burstTalentLevel": 10
      }
